{"title":"Career roadmap · Financial Analyst (Junior)","role":"Financial Analyst (Junior)","summary":"Career alignment:\nB.Com General provides a strong foundation for junior financial-analysis roles because it covers accounting, business, economics and finance. To become job-ready, the student should add financial modelling, Excel, accounting analysis, financial statements, valuation basics, Power BI/SQL and business communication.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–1 year"},{"text":"Finance Intern, Finance Executive, Junior Financial Analyst"}],[{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Financial Analyst, FP&A Analyst, Investment Operations Analyst"}],[{"text":"3–5 years"},{"text":"Senior Financial Analyst, FP&A Analyst, Business Finance Analyst"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Finance Manager, FP&A Manager, Corporate Finance Manager"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Finance Director, Head of FP&A, Finance Controller, CFO-track roles"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Com","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Commerce & Accounting Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Accounting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Journal entries"},{"text":"Ledger and trial balance"},{"text":"Profit & loss statement"},{"text":"Balance sheet"},{"text":"Cash-flow statement"},{"text":"Depreciation"},{"text":"Working capital"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Accounts receivable/payable"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Economics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microeconomics"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Inflation"},{"text":"Interest rates"},{"text":"GDP"},{"text":"Monetary/fiscal policy"},{"text":"Business cycles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Business fundamentals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Business organisations"},{"text":"Corporate finance basics"},{"text":"Business mathema